<cell id="cell-0"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type># M7 L7: Retrieval and Ranking

**Build BM25, dense cosine, RRF, and MMR from scratch.  Hybrid wins.**

Duration: 90 min.  No API keys.</cell id="cell-0>
<cell id="cell-1"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## Plain English (the 12-year-old version)

**Retrieval** means: given a question, find the most relevant documents to feed to the AI.

There are three main ways: **BM25** (count exact word matches — good for "SKU-12345"), **dense cosine** (compare the *meaning* — good for "kitten" vs "cat"), and **hybrid** (do both). Hybrid wins on most real-world collections.

When the top results are all saying the same thing, use **MMR** to pick a diverse set. When results are still not good enough, add a **reranker** — a slower, smarter model that reads the question and each result pair-by-pair.</cell id="cell-1>
<cell id="cell-2"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## The 5 things to know

1. **BM25** catches exact matches; **dense** catches semantic similarity.
2. **Hybrid wins** — usually 10-20 points of recall better than either alone.
3. **RRF** is the standard merge — one line of code, no tuning.
4. **MMR** diversifies the result list; lambda controls the relevance/diversity trade-off.
5. **Cross-encoder reranker** is the next upgrade if recall@K is below target.</cell id="cell-2>
<cell id="cell-3"># === Standard setup ===
import sys, importlib.util
from pathlib import Path

def find_root(p):
    while p != p.parent:
        if (p / 'lessons').exists() and (p / 'SYLLABUS.md').exists():
            return p
        p = p.parent
    return Path.cwd()

ROOT = find_root(Path.cwd())
sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))

_p = ROOT / 'lessons' / 'm07-retrieval' / 'L7-retrieval-ranking.py'
_spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('L7', _p)
_L7 = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)
sys.modules['L7'] = _L7
_spec.loader.exec_module(_L7)

print(f'Setup OK. Lesson module: {_L7.LESSON_NUMBER}')</cell id="cell-3>
<cell id="cell-4"># Run the 10 unit tests inline
import inspect
tests = [(n, fn) for n, fn in inspect.getmembers(_L7, inspect.isfunction) if n.startswith('test_')]
print(f'Running {len(tests)} tests...\n')
passed, failed = 0, 0
for name, fn in tests:
    try:
        fn()
        print(f'  PASS  {name}')
        passed += 1
    except AssertionError as e:
        print(f'  FAIL  {name}: {e}')
        failed += 1
print(f'\n{passed}/{len(tests)} tests pass, {failed} fail')
assert failed == 0, f'{failed} test(s) failed -- fix before continuing'</cell id="cell-4>
<cell id="cell-5"># === Section 1: BM25 on the 4 sample queries ===
bm = _L7.BM25()
bm.fit(_L7.SAMPLE_DOCS)
print(f'{"query":<48}  top-3 (BM25)')
for q, _ in _L7.SAMPLE_QUERIES:
    hits = bm.score(q)[:3]
    ids = [i for i, _ in hits]
    print(f'  {q!r:<46}  {ids}')</cell id="cell-5>
<cell id="cell-6"># === Section 2: dense cosine on the same queries ===
de = _L7.Dense()
de.fit(_L7.SAMPLE_DOCS)
print(f'{"query":<48}  top-3 (dense)')
for q, _ in _L7.SAMPLE_QUERIES:
    hits = de.score(q)[:3]
    ids = [i for i, _ in hits]
    print(f'  {q!r:<46}  {ids}')</cell id="cell-6>
<cell id="cell-7"># === Section 3: RRF (Reciprocal Rank Fusion) ===
print(f'{"query":<48}  top-5 (RRF)')
for q, _ in _L7.SAMPLE_QUERIES:
    bm_hits = bm.score(q)[:10]
    de_hits = de.score(q)[:10]
    merged = _L7.rrf([bm_hits, de_hits], k=_L7.RRF_K)[:5]
    ids = [i for i, _ in merged]
    print(f'  {q!r:<46}  {ids}')</cell id="cell-7>
<cell id="cell-8"># === Section 4: RRF with weighted rankings (2x dense) ===
print(f'{"query":<48}  top-5 (RRF, 2x dense weight)')
for q, _ in _L7.SAMPLE_QUERIES:
    bm_hits = bm.score(q)[:10]
    de_hits = de.score(q)[:10]
    merged = _L7.rrf([bm_hits, de_hits, de_hits], k=_L7.RRF_K)[:5]
    ids = [i for i, _ in merged]
    print(f'  {q!r:<46}  {ids}')</cell id="cell-8>
<cell id="cell-9"># === Section 5: MMR diversification (lambda=0.5) ===
import numpy as np
q, _ = _L7.SAMPLE_QUERIES[0]
qv = _L7.fake_embed(q)
cand_ids = [i for i, _ in de.score(q)[:20]]
selected = _L7.mmr(qv, de.vectors, cand_ids, lambda_=0.5, k=5)
print(f'query: {q!r}')
print(f'selected (in order): {selected}')
print(f'selected texts:')
for i in selected:
    print(f'  [{i}] {_L7.SAMPLE_DOCS[i][:60]!r}')</cell id="cell-9>
<cell id="cell-10"># === Section 6: MMR lambda sweep (diversity vs relevance) ===
print('Sweep lambda on MMR; report mean pairwise sim in top-5:\n')
for lam in (0.0, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 1.0):
    sel = _L7.mmr(qv, de.vectors, cand_ids, lambda_=lam, k=5)
    # mean pairwise sim in selected
    if len(sel) > 1:
        sims = []
        for a in sel:
            for b in sel:
                if a < b:
                    sims.append(float(np.dot(de.vectors[a], de.vectors[b])))
        mean_sim = sum(sims) / len(sims) if sims else 0
    else:
        mean_sim = 0
    print(f'  lambda={lam:.1f}  selected={sel}  mean_pair_sim={mean_sim:.3f}')</cell id="cell-10>
<cell id="cell-11"># === Section 7: recall@3 comparison ===
print('Mean recall@3 on the 4 sample queries:\n')
for label, fn in (
    ('BM25',  bm.score),
    ('Dense', de.score),
    ('RRF',   lambda q: _L7.rrf([bm.score(q), de.score(q)], k=_L7.RRF_K)),
):
    recall = 0
    for q, expected in _L7.SAMPLE_QUERIES:
        hits = fn(q)[:3]
        ids = [i for i, _ in hits]
        if int(expected) in ids:
            recall += 1
    print(f'  {label:<6}  recall@3 = {recall/len(_L7.SAMPLE_QUERIES):.2f}')</cell id="cell-11>
<cell id="cell-12"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## Architecture (Mermaid)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Q[query] --> BM[BM25<br/>sparse lexical]
    Q --> DE[Dense cosine<br/>semantic]
    BM --> T1[top-N BM25 hits]
    DE --> T2[top-N dense hits]
    T1 --> RRF[RRF merge<br/>1 / k+rank]
    T2 --> RRF
    RRF --> M[merged top-K]
    M --> MMR{MMR?<br/>diversify}
    MMR -->|no| OUT[final top-K]
    MMR -->|yes| DIV[diverse top-K]
    DIV --> OUT
```

**Read as:** Run both retrievers in parallel, merge with RRF, optionally diversify with MMR.</cell id="cell-12>
